node_modules/
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build outputs. Regenerate with `node scripts/build.mjs` /
# `node scripts/repro_build.mjs`. The reproducible parts are pinned by hash in
# supply-chain/artifacts.lock.json, so a reviewer can verify a rebuild without
# these being committed. 406 MB of derived artefacts do not belong in git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/*
build-repro/
build-repro-2/
circuits/*_js/
circuits/*.r1cs
circuits/*.sym
scratch_mem/

# ...but DO publish the verification keys: they are small, they are what a
# verifier actually needs, and without them nobody can check a proof.
!build/*_vkey.json

# The browser demo in web/ IS published (wasm + evaluation-only zkeys + vkeys)
# so the "verify it yourself" quickstart works out of the box. See web/README.md
# and NOTICE: those proving keys are from a throwaway single-contribution setup
# and are for EVALUATION ONLY, never production.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not published: business material (pricing, revenue, moat, competitive
# strategy, go-to-market). Everything technical is public.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARTNER-BRIEF.md
../private-business-notes/
**/the-open-source-moat.md
**/playing-against-giants.md
**/surviving-due-diligence.md

# paper build intermediates (the PDF itself IS committed)
paper/_built.html
paper/_chart*.svg
paper/_proof.json
paper/_appendixA.txt
paper/_figs.*
paper/_vp.txt
paper/_paperproof.json
